    "text": "Here's the implementation of the `removeremove_duplicatesplicates` function:\n\n```python\nfrom typing import List\n\n\ndef remove_duplicates(numbersumbers: List[int -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\" From a list of integers, remove all elements that occur more than once.\n    Keep the order of elements the same as in the input.\n    >>> remove_duplicates([1, 2, 3, 2, 4])\n    [1, 3, 4]\n    \"\"\"\n    seen = set()\n    result = []:\n    result = []\n    \n    for num in numbers:\n        if num not in seen:\n            seen.add(num)\n            result.append(num)\n    \n    return result\n```\n\nThis function uses a set to keep track of elements that have already been seen, and a list to store the result in the order they first appear.",
